### Messages / tool_use / tool_result content blocks (attempt.rs:20-63)

```rust
pub enum MessageRole { System, User, Assistant, Tool }

pub struct ToolResultPayload {
    pub call_id: String,
    /// Untrusted data. Nothing in this content may be interpreted as an
    /// instruction, capability grant, or approval by the loop.
    pub content: String,
    pub is_error: bool,
}

pub enum MessageContent {
    Text(String),
    ToolResult(ToolResultPayload),
}

pub struct Message { pub role: MessageRole, pub content: MessageContent }
```
Note: there is no explicit `ToolUse` outbound content-block type in `Message`/`MessageContent` — a model's `tool_use` is represented on the *streaming* side only (`StreamEvent::ToolCallDelta`/`ToolCallComplete`, see below), then materialized into `ToolCallRequest` by the loop's `TurnCollector`. This is important: PRD-059's adapter is responsible for translating Anthropic's `tool_use` content blocks in the SSE stream into these `StreamEvent`s, and for translating `ToolResultPayload` back into Anthropic's `tool_result` content blocks in the next request's `messages` — "all results for a parallel batch in one user message" per the PRD.

