### Test double — `FakeInferenceAdapter` / `ScriptedTurn` (attempt.rs:251-318)
The reference/offline implementation your fixture suite should mirror the pattern of:
```rust
pub struct ScriptedTurn {
    pub events: Vec<StreamEvent>,
    pub outcome: Result<SubmitOutcome, AdapterError>,
}
pub struct FakeInferenceAdapter { turns: Mutex<VecDeque<ScriptedTurn>>, cancelled: Mutex<Vec<AttemptId>> }
```
It's used both in-crate and by `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/raw_runtime.rs`. Your `anthropic_api.rs`'s wiremock-based tests are a *different, additional* layer that exercises the real Anthropic wire format; `FakeInferenceAdapter` stays the no-network double for loop-level tests.

### Cancellation (raw_runtime.rs:732-747)
```rust
pub struct CancellationToken(Arc<AtomicBool>);
impl CancellationToken {
    pub fn new() -> Self { .. }
    pub fn cancel(&self) { .. }
    pub fn is_cancelled(&self) -> bool { .. }
}
```
Cooperative only; loop checks it every iteration (`raw_runtime.rs:868-869`) and wraps `adapter.submit()` in `tokio::time::timeout` when a wall-clock ceiling is configured (`raw_runtime.rs:895-915`), converting a timeout into `StopReason::Timeout` with `AttemptUsage { ambiguous: true, usage: UsageCategories::default() }` — this is the exact mechanism PRD-059's acceptance criterion #10 ("a timeout with unknown completion records ambiguous usage") relies on; the adapter itself doesn't need to implement this, the loop does it around `submit()`.

### Retries/attempts model (raw_runtime.rs:830-834, 940-945)
- `run_loop` takes `mint_attempt_id: impl FnMut() -> AttemptId` — **every submission mints a fresh `AttemptId`**; there is no adapter-internal retry. `AttemptUsage { attempt_id, usage, ambiguous }` is recorded per attempt regardless of outcome.
- Tool capability/validation/authorization/journal machinery (`CapabilityId`, `ToolCapability`, `ValidatedCall`, `ToolAuthorizer`, `ToolJournal`, `ScopeAuthorizer`, `resume_decision_for`) is entirely orthogonal to PRD-059 — none of it needs to change; PRD-059 only plugs a new `InferenceAdapter` impl in.

