## 2. familiar-ai-llm/src/attempt.rs — "attempt" model

Already fully quoted above. Summary of the model:
- **`AttemptId(String)`** — globally unique per submission, minted fresh even for a retry of the same logical turn (comment at attempt.rs:10-12).
- **`ReservationId(String)`** — "A PRD-064 budget reservation bound to exactly one `AttemptId`" (attempt.rs:16-18). This type is declared here but the actual reservation *acquire/settle* mechanics live in `crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/repos/reservation.rs` (PRD-064's `ReservationRepository`), which is provider-agnostic resource-pool bookkeeping (nanoUSD budget, token pools, inference slots) — see item 9 below for its shape. `attempt.rs` itself does **not** call into `reservation.rs`; that wiring, if any, would happen at the daemon/host layer around `run_loop`, not inside the adapter.
- Each `submit()` call is one attempt; `AttemptUsage` (in `raw_runtime.rs:715-722`) pairs an `AttemptId` with `UsageCategories` and an `ambiguous: bool` flag for provider-timeout-with-unknown-completion cases.

