**No existing `anthropic.rs` stub or partial content** — confirmed both by directory listing and by the crate's `mod` declarations.

**Two distinct "adapter" registration patterns exist in this crate, and they are for different runtimes:**
1. **`registry.rs`'s `AdapterFactory`/`AdapterFactories`** — for CLI-harness workers (Claude Code, Codex). Keyed by `runtime_id` string, builds `Box<dyn CodingAgent>`:
   ```rust
   pub trait AdapterFactory: Send + Sync {
       fn adapter_id(&self) -> &str;
       fn build(&self, worker: &WorkerDescriptor) -> Result<Box<dyn CodingAgent>, String>;
   }
   pub struct AdapterFactories { factories: BTreeMap<String, Box<dyn AdapterFactory>> }
   impl AdapterFactories {
       pub fn build(&self, worker: &WorkerDescriptor) -> Result<Box<dyn CodingAgent>, String> {
           self.factories.get(&worker.runtime_id)...build(worker)
       }
   }
   ```
   This is **not** the mechanism PRD-059 plugs into — `anthropic-api` is a raw runtime speaking `InferenceAdapter`, not a `CodingAgent` subprocess harness. Do not register it here.
2. **No equivalent registry/factory exists yet for `InferenceAdapter`** — confirmed in item 10 below: the daemon and agent crates currently only ever construct `FakeInferenceAdapter` directly in tests; there is no `"anthropic-api" -> Box<dyn InferenceAdapter>` factory anywhere. **PRD-059 will need to introduce this wiring itself** (likely a small function/registry in `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs` and/or daemon-side code, following the `AdapterFactories` naming convention loosely but keyed to `InferenceAdapter` rather than `CodingAgent`).

