}

pub enum EndpointProviderKind { Inference, DeployTarget, Billing }

pub enum BillingMode {
    AnthropicOrganization, OpenAiOrganization, Bedrock, Vertex, Foundry, ExternalBilling,
}

pub enum InferenceRuntimeKind { Unsloth }   // <-- only one runtime kind exists today; anthropic-api is absent

pub enum AuthDescriptor {
    None, CliLogin(String), Env(String), CredentialStore(CredentialStoreDescriptor), SshAgent,
}
```

**Key finding: `InferenceRuntimeKind` currently only has `Unsloth`.** PRD-059 needs to decide whether `anthropic-api` needs its own `InferenceRuntimeKind` variant here, or whether (more likely, per PRD-057's design) the worker's `runtime` string lives in `RegistryWorkerConfig.runtime: Option<String>` (in `registry_workers.rs`, an untyped string validated only by identifier rules, not a closed enum) rather than in `ProviderConfig.runtime: Option<InferenceRuntimeKind>` — the latter field's doc comment says "Deploy-target executable... Absent selects legacy SSH transport" is for `via`, but `runtime: Option<InferenceRuntimeKind>` appears to be scoped narrowly to the Unsloth deploy-target use case per its validation rules (`EndpointProviderKind::Inference` provider validation doesn't reference `runtime` at all in the `validate()` match arms shown — worth re-checking at implementation time whether `runtime` is even meaningful for a `kind = "inference"` Anthropic provider entry, or whether Anthropic's provider config just needs `kind = Inference`, `host`, `auth`, `models` with no runtime tag, and the runtime tag lives purely on the *worker* side in `registry_workers.rs`).

`ProviderConfig::validate()` (providers.rs:169-293) enforces per-`kind` invariants — e.g. an `Inference` provider must not set `billing_mode`/`organization_id`/`recipe`/`capabilities`/`via`. Any new fields PRD-059 adds must respect `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` and this closed validation.

**Companion file — `agent_runtime.rs` capability-profile-adjacent config** (`crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/agent_runtime.rs`, full file read): defines `AgentRuntimeConfig` (loop-level, not provider-level — `enabled`, `offered_capabilities: Vec<String>` validated against `AGENT_RUNTIME_CAPABILITIES` (a hardcoded mirror of `CapabilityId::as_str()` since core can't depend on the agent crate), `AgentRuntimeCeilingsConfig`, `AgentRuntimeSandboxConfig` (`allowed_commands`, `network_allowed`, `allowed_environment` with `FORBIDDEN_ENVIRONMENT_MARKERS = ["BILLING","ADMIN","STRIPE","PAYMENT","ROOT_"]` fail-closed check)). This is the config PRD-059's Anthropic worker would reference for tool offering/ceilings, but it's runtime-agnostic — no changes needed here for PRD-059 unless capability-profile-per-provider defaults are added.

**The actual "capability profile" concept** lives in a different file — `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs` — see item 7 below.

