## 6. docs/contracts/agent-loop.md

Full file read (229 lines). Section-by-section summary:

- **State machine** (line 46-77): `compose -> submit -> streaming turn -> {text|tool calls|structured output|stop} -> validate -> authorize -> execute (journaled) -> insert results -> iterate | terminal`. Explicitly: "Usage for the attempt is the adapter's final reported total, never derived by summing deltas" (line 61-62) — **this means PRD-059's `SubmitOutcome.usage` must be the authoritative final total from Anthropic's terminal `message_delta`/`message_stop` usage block, not a sum of streamed `UsageDelta` events**, even though the adapter also emits `StreamEvent::UsageDelta` along the way for observers.
- **Canonical tool capabilities table** (line 79-98): the 7 capabilities (`read-file`, `search-list`, `run-command`, `apply-edit`, `report-progress`, `submit-evidence`, `request-escalation`) with side-effect classes; explicit: a projection (including a "native provider tool definition") "**MAY** narrow this set... it **MUST NOT** widen it or invent a capability outside this table." PRD-059's native Anthropic tool projection must map 1:1 (or a subset) onto exactly these 7 capability ids — no extra tools.
- **Inference adapter contract section** (line 100-122) — this is the normative doc-form of the trait I quoted in #1, explicitly states: "Adding an adapter is configuration plus an `InferenceAdapter` implementation; it changes no loop, authority, or persistence semantics" — directly matches PRD-059's first acceptance criterion.
- **Write-ahead tool journal** (line 124-148): intent-before-execution durability rule and the `resume_decision_for` table (read-only/idempotent-write replay allowed, destructive fails closed). Journal entries key on the **model-issued call id**, not the inference attempt — "A provider-level retry that produces the *same* tool call is not a new journal entry merely because the inference attempt differs." Relevant to PRD-059 because a retried Anthropic request that re-issues the same `tool_use.id` must map back to the same journal call_id.
- **Write-scope authorization** (line 150-164): PRD-013-Expected-Files-derived write allowlist; `run-command` gated by `argv[0]` allowlist. Not adapter-specific.
- **Authority and sandboxing** (line 166-188): no ambient authority; environment allowlist-only; filesystem worktree-confined; network deny-by-default; cancellation kills process groups; **"No tool result and no model output can grant a capability, raise authority, or approve anything"** — i.e., PRD-059's adapter must never let Anthropic's response content (including thinking blocks or refusals) be treated as anything but untrusted `ToolResult`/text data.
- **Stop reasons** (line 190-201): the closed `StopReason` enum (quoted in #1) plus the invariant "a provider error is never relabeled `TokenOrContextCeiling`, and a fatal tool refusal is never recorded as `Completed`" — directly matches PRD-059 acceptance criterion #6 about refusal stops being honest terminal reasons.
- **Evidence and accounting** (line 203-220): Evidence tables (`agent_runtime_evidence`, `agent_runtime_tool_intents`, `agent_runtime_tool_results`, migration 055) reconstruct disposition/stop-reason/resume-point deterministically and must never carry prompt/response/source/tool-output content. **PRD-051 usage lands via `familiar_ai_daemon::agent_runtime::persist_run_outcome`, which calls `AccountingRepository::append_observation` for every attempt** — same ledger every execution uses (see #9/#10 below for exact signatures). "An accounting row **MUST NOT** ever carry a prompt, a response, source code, or tool output." An attempt with entirely unknown usage records an explicit `unknown_reason`, never a fabricated zero.
- **Test harness** (line 222-229): every test in `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/raw_runtime.rs` and `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/raw_runtime.rs` runs exclusively against `FakeInferenceAdapter` — "No test in either file performs, or is able to perform, a live or billable call." PRD-059's own test files (`crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/anthropic.rs`, `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/anthropic_adapter.rs`) should follow the identical no-network-except-wiremock discipline.
- **Explicit non-goal** (line 33-38): "Real hosted provider wire adapters (Anthropic/OpenAI/xAI/local-runtime HTTP clients). This contract defines the adapter trait every such client implements; shipping one is configuration plus adapter work under the PRD-057 contract, not a change to this document." — confirms PRD-059 should not need to modify `agent-loop.md`'s normative content, only reference it, unless there's a doc gap (e.g., no mention yet of cache_control breakpoint placement specifics, thinking-block replay rules, or the closed `AdapterStopReason` list at the wire-mapping level — those belong in the new `docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md`).

