### Insert function signature (accounting.rs:607-645)

```rust
/// Idempotency is keyed by the sanitized source-event hash. Evidence and
/// its observation commit atomically; replay returns the existing
/// observation so a missing idempotent cost fact can still be repaired.
pub fn append_observation(
    &self,
    value: &UsageObservation<'_>,
) -> familiar_ai_core::Result<Option<String>> {
    // idempotency check: SELECT observation_id ... JOIN accounting_evidence ON evidence.source_event_hash=?1
    // if found -> return Ok(Some(existing))  [replay is idempotent]
    // else: mints evi_<hex>/obs_<hex>, resolves project via resolve_project(project_resolution_evidence),
    //   looks up spec_identity/empirical_version from worker_selections (execution_id, stage) latest row,
    //   INSERTs into accounting_evidence(...) then usage_observations(...) inside one transaction, commits.
}
```
This is the exact idempotent-replay mechanism referenced in PRD-059's acceptance criterion: "replay of the same persisted provider event is idempotent while separate billable attempts remain separate observations" — **`source_event_hash` is the idempotency key**; the daemon-side caller (`persist_run_outcome`, see #10) currently computes it as `sha256_hex(execution_id + ":" + attempt_id)` — since every attempt already has a unique `AttemptId`, this naturally gives "separate billable attempts remain separate observations" for free, and a provider idempotency key/`provider_request_id` replay would need to reuse the *same* `attempt_id`/hash to be treated as the same event.

### Related cost-estimate append functions (accounting.rs:647-691, see #12 for full detail)
`append_vendor_estimate`, `append_legacy_configured_estimate`, `append_credit_estimate` — these are how a `UsageObservation`'s tokens get turned into a `local-estimate` nanoUSD cost row via `cost_estimates` (append-only, `UNIQUE(observation_id, provenance)`), keyed to a `price_schedules` row.

