**`crates/familiar-ai-core/Cargo.toml`**: thiserror, serde, figment, toml, chrono, dirs, libc, tracing, serde_json, ring. **No reqwest, no tokio, no async-trait, no wiremock.** (Core stays foundational/sync — consistent with the comment in `attempt.rs` that core has no dependency on the agent crate.)

**`crates/familiar-ai-llm/Cargo.toml`**: already has `familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-tokens`, `async-trait`, `tokio` (sync/rt/time/macros features), `tracing`, `thiserror`, `serde`, `serde_json`, **`reqwest`**, `chrono`. Dev-deps: **`wiremock`**, `tokio` (full + test-util). — **This crate is fully equipped for `anthropic_api.rs` today, zero Cargo.toml changes needed** for the HTTP+SSE+wiremock work.

**`crates/familiar-ai-agent/Cargo.toml`**: `familiar-ai-llm` (path dep), serde_json, libc, ring, tokio (time/macros/rt). Linux-only `landlock`. Dev-deps: tempfile, tokio (macros/rt/rt-multi-thread). **No reqwest, no wiremock, no async-trait declared directly** (transitively available via `familiar-ai-llm` but not usable directly unless re-exported or added). Since `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/anthropic.rs` is an expected file and will presumably want to build a real `wiremock::MockServer` and feed it into an adapter constructed via `familiar_ai_llm::anthropic_api`, **you will likely need to add `wiremock` (and possibly `reqwest`) to `familiar-ai-agent`'s `[dev-dependencies]`** unless that test only exercises the loop with a `FakeInferenceAdapter`-style double and leaves wire-level testing entirely to `familiar-ai-llm`'s own tests.

**`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/Cargo.toml`**: has `tokio.workspace`, `reqwest.workspace` in `[dependencies]`. Dev-deps: `familiar-ai-testutil`, `tempfile`, `assert_cmd`, `predicates`, `nix`. **No `wiremock` dev-dependency today** — if `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/anthropic_adapter.rs` needs to mock HTTP directly (rather than just exercising `persist_run_outcome` against a `FakeInferenceAdapter`-produced `RunOutcome`, which needs no HTTP mocking at all), you'll need to add `wiremock` to daemon's dev-deps too. Given the existing `raw_runtime.rs` daemon test pattern uses `FakeInferenceAdapter` exclusively (no wiremock), the more likely/consistent design is that `anthropic_adapter.rs` in the daemon crate also just drives `persist_run_outcome`/`run_loop` with either `FakeInferenceAdapter` or a thin fixture-backed `InferenceAdapter`, while true HTTP-wire tests live in `familiar-ai-llm`'s own `#[cfg(test)]` module (matching `openai_http.rs`'s pattern) or in `familiar-ai-agent/tests/anthropic.rs`.

**Existing HTTP client conventions elsewhere in the workspace:**
