## 13. docs/contracts/credential-authentication.md and credential resolution code

**Doc content** (full, 13 lines, quoted in #7): BYO-Auth only, diagnostic descriptor forms (CLI login / env-var name / SSH agent / `none`), never a credential value in config/args/logs/reports/comments/DB rows.

**The "exact BYO-Auth remedy" pattern** — there is no single canonical remedy string constant shared across the whole workspace; each call site defines its own precise remedy text, but they all follow the same shape ("<what's wrong> — <exact operator action>"). Concrete instances found:

1. **Generic auth-profile-missing remedy** — `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/mod.rs:456-464`:
   ```rust
   format!("worker_registry.workers.{id} auth profile '{profile}' is missing; configure [auth_profiles.{profile}] with a BYO-Auth descriptor")
   ```
2. **CLI-level generic remedy constant** — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/config_cli.rs:24-25`:
   ```rust
   const BYO_AUTH_REMEDY: &str =
       "configure BYO-auth with a descriptor (`cli-login: NAME`, `env: NAME`, `credential-store: STORE/SERVICE/ACCOUNT`, `ssh-agent`, or `none`); never pass a credential";
   ```
3. **Billing-specific remedy constants** — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/billing.rs:8-13`:
   ```rust
   pub const INDIVIDUAL_REMEDY: &str = "credential lacks organization authority — individual API accounts have no Admin API; view billing in the Claude Console, or supply an organization Admin key";
   pub const MISSING_CREDENTIAL_REMEDY: &str = "billing credential reference is unavailable — export the referenced organization Admin key";
   pub const EXPIRED_CREDENTIAL_REMEDY: &str = "billing credential is expired or invalid — replace the referenced organization Admin key";
   pub const INSUFFICIENT_ROLE_REMEDY: &str = "credential has insufficient role — supply an organization Admin key with billing read authority";
   pub const EXTERNAL_REMEDY: &str = "external billing collector unsupported — local-estimate-only coverage until a dedicated PRD authorizes a collector";
   ```
   These are the closest existing precedent for an *Anthropic-specific* remedy string; PRD-059's inference-side auth failure (401/403 from `/v1/messages`) should mint an analogous constant, e.g. something like `"anthropic API credential is missing or invalid — export the referenced env var (or fix the credential-store entry) named by the worker's auth_profile"`, mapped into `AdapterError::NonRetryable(NonRetryableKind::Auth)`.

**Where credential resolution code currently lives:**
- **`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/config_cli.rs:27-140`** — the most general-purpose, reusable resolver:
  ```rust
  pub trait CredentialStore {
      fn resolve(&self, descriptor: &CredentialStoreDescriptor) -> Result<String, CredentialStoreError>;
  }
  pub enum CredentialStoreError { UnsupportedPlatform, Missing, AccessDenied, Unavailable }
  pub struct SystemCredentialStore;   // macOS Keychain via `/usr/bin/security find-generic-password`
  pub struct ResolvedCredential(String);  // Debug redacts to "[REDACTED]"
  impl ResolvedCredential { pub fn expose_for_request(&self) -> &str { &self.0 } }
  pub fn resolve_auth_with_store(auth: &AuthDescriptor, store: &dyn CredentialStore) -> Result<Option<ResolvedCredential>, String> {
      match auth {
          AuthDescriptor::Env(name) => std::env::var(name).ok().filter(|v| !v.is_empty())
              .map(ResolvedCredential).map(Some)
              .ok_or_else(|| format!("required environment variable {name} is missing — export `{name}`.")),
          AuthDescriptor::CredentialStore(descriptor) => store.resolve(descriptor)...,
          ... 
      }
  }
  ```
  This lives in the **daemon** crate, not in `familiar-ai-core` or `familiar-ai-llm` — meaning **PRD-059's `anthropic_api.rs` (in `familiar-ai-llm`, which cannot depend on the daemon crate) cannot reuse `resolve_auth_with_store` directly.** Either (a) the daemon resolves the credential and passes a bare `&str`/`ResolvedCredential`-like type into the adapter constructor at wiring time (most likely, matching "credentials exist only as external references resolved at call time in the adapter boundary" from the PRD — the "adapter boundary" is ambiguous whether it means the `InferenceAdapter` impl itself or the daemon-side construction point), or (b) a smaller, duplicate `AuthDescriptor::Env`-only resolver gets added directly inside `familiar-ai-llm` (simpler, avoids a new inter-crate dependency, matches the narrower pattern already used standalone in `billing.rs:292-303`'s private `fn credential(auth: &AuthDescriptor) -> Result<String, String>`).
- **`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/billing.rs:292-303`** — narrower, billing-specific, `Env`-only (rejects any other `AuthDescriptor` variant): the simplest possible reference implementation, worth copying verbatim in spirit for an Anthropic-inference-key resolver if a minimal `env:`-only resolver is what's wanted (Anthropic API keys are near-universally supplied via `env: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`-style descriptors in practice).
- **Redaction pattern**: `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/agent.rs` exports `redact_sensitive` (re-exported from `lib.rs`) — worth checking as a possible existing helper for scrubbing the API key out of error messages/evidence before PRD-059 writes its own; not read in full but present and public.
- **Environment scrubbing precedent**: `billing.rs:22-31`'s `scrub_credentials_from_process_environment` removes billing env vars from the *ambient* process before spawning any subprocess — analogous to `agent_runtime.rs`'s `SandboxedToolExecutor::run_command`'s `command.env_clear()` + explicit allowlist (line 306-311) which already enforces "tool subprocess environments never inherit it" for the raw-runtime loop generically; PRD-059 doesn't need to add anything new here since `run-command` tool execution already never inherits ambient env, and the Anthropic API key never needs to reach a tool subprocess at all (it's only used by the adapter's own `reqwest::Client`, in-process).

---

## 14. Test fixture/mocking conventions — wiremock usage

**Confirmed**: `wiremock` is the workspace's HTTP-mocking library (declared at workspace root, `wiremock = "0.6"`). `mockito`/`httpmock` are **not used anywhere** in the repo (grep for all three found zero mockito/httpmock hits).

**Only one Cargo.toml currently pulls in wiremock as a dev-dependency**: `crates/familiar-ai-llm/Cargo.toml` (`wiremock.workspace = true` under `[dev-dependencies]`).

**The complete worked example** is `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/backends/openai_http.rs`'s `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (lines 299-605, read in full in #3) — representative pattern to copy verbatim for `anthropic_api.rs`:

```rust
use wiremock::matchers::{header, method, path};
use wiremock::{Mock, MockServer, ResponseTemplate};

#[tokio::test]
async fn health_check_200_is_healthy() {
    let server = MockServer::start().await;
    Mock::given(method("GET"))
        .and(path("/models"))
        .respond_with(ResponseTemplate::new(200).set_body_json(json!({"data": []})))
        .mount(&server)
        .await;

    let backend = OpenAiHttpBackend::new(default_config(server.uri())).unwrap();
    let health = backend.health_check().await.unwrap();
    assert_eq!(health, HealthStatus::Healthy);
}
```
Other useful matcher/assertion idioms demonstrated in the same file: matching a request header (`.and(header("authorization", "Bearer sk-test"))` for auth-key propagation tests — directly reusable for asserting the Anthropic adapter sends `x-api-key`/`anthropic-version` correctly), simulating various HTTP status codes (401/403/404/429/500) mapped to distinct error variants, and simulating connection failure by pointing at an unused port (`http://127.0.0.1:1`) rather than mocking a transport error directly.

**No SSE/streaming-response wiremock example exists yet anywhere in the repo** — all current wiremock usage is against simple JSON request/response bodies (`set_body_json`). PRD-059 will be the first to need a streaming `text/event-stream` mock; wiremock 0.6 supports arbitrary response bodies via `ResponseTemplate::new(200).set_body_raw(bytes, "text/event-stream")` or `.set_body_string(sse_payload)`, so the existing infrastructure supports it, it's just not yet exercised in this codebase — worth flagging as genuinely new ground you'll be breaking.

**Daemon-crate precedent for driving the loop end-to-end without any HTTP mocking** (since it never needs real wire traffic — the daemon only ever talks to `dyn InferenceAdapter`, and the reference no-network double is `FakeInferenceAdapter`): `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/raw_runtime.rs` (read first 150 of 708 lines, full pattern shown in #10). This is the shape `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/anthropic_adapter.rs` should follow for its persistence-layer assertions (SQLite in-memory `Database::open_in_memory()`, `run_migrations()`, `setup_execution(...)` helper inserting a fake `execution_history` row, then `run_loop(...)` + `persist_run_outcome(...)` + direct SQL/`AgentRuntimeRepository` assertions on what landed).
