## Summary

Implemented PRD-059 (Anthropic Raw-API Inference Adapter):

**New files** (all expected_files):
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/anthropic_api.rs` — wire-level HTTP/SSE client (request/response shapes, streaming, error taxonomy classification, non-billable `count_tokens`/`retrieve_model` probes, BYO-Auth credential resolution)
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/anthropic.rs` — the `InferenceAdapter` implementation (tool projection, `tool_use`/`tool_result`/thinking-block reconstruction across turns, cache-control placement, stop-reason mapping)
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/anthropic.rs` and `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/anthropic_adapter.rs` — deterministic wiremock-backed fixture suites
- `docs/contracts/anthropic-adapter.md` — the normative contract, including two documented design decisions

**Modified**: `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/providers.rs` (capability-profile defaults + runtime const), `config/default.toml` (worked example + dated price schedule), plus small additive fixes required for honesty: `AdapterStopReason` gained `PauseTurn`/`Refusal` variants (Anthropic's `pause_turn`/`refusal` had no correct existing mapping), and `AttemptUsage` gained `provider_request_id` (previously dropped on the floor for every adapter). Both were minimal, backward-compatible, and verified against the full existing PRD-058 test suite, which still passes unchanged.

Every acceptance criterion is met and tested. One pre-existing environment limitation: the sandbox lacks `libxdo` (X11), so the default `tray` feature fails to link — unrelated to this PRD; all testing was done with `--no-default-features`.

No incomplete acceptance criteria — nothing to flag as `FAMILIAR-INCOMPLETE`.
