## Summary

Implemented PRD-060 (OpenAI Raw-API Inference Adapter) as the first concrete adapter built on the PRD-058 `InferenceAdapter` contract (its sibling, PRD-059/Anthropic, doesn't exist yet, so there was no precedent to mirror — everything here was designed from the PRD-058 contract and the current Responses API shape).

**New files:**
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs` — Responses API wire client: request building, SSE event parsing/mapping, error taxonomy, usage normalization. 24 unit tests against `wiremock`.
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/openai.rs` — `OpenAiInferenceAdapter` implementing `InferenceAdapter`; per-attempt metadata (resolved model, service tier, provider request id) recorded for host enrichment.
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/openai.rs` — 12 tests driving the real PRD-058 `run_loop` against the adapter.
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/openai_adapter.rs` — 6 tests: full SQLite-backed loop + shared `persist_run_outcome`, ledger enrichment, exactly-once idempotent replay, versioned price-schedule reconciliation, BYO-Auth resolution.
- `docs/contracts/openai-adapter.md` — normative adapter contract.

**Modified:** `familiar-ai-agent`/`familiar-ai-llm`/`familiar-ai-daemon` `Cargo.toml`/`lib.rs` (module registration, `async-trait` and `wiremock` dev-dep additions only).

**Verified during implementation (2026-09-01), correcting the PRD's 2026-08-30 design note:** OpenAI's Responses API *does* now report `input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens`. The adapter records it distinctly rather than treating it as always-absent — documented prominently in both the code and the contract doc as a headline correction, not a footnote.

**Deliberate scope decisions (not gaps):**
1. `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/providers.rs` (listed in expected_files) was **not modified** — its existing generic `Inference`/`Billing` provider kinds already fully accommodate an OpenAI endpoint and a separate Admin billing source; no acceptance criterion required a new field there.
2. No generic "price-schedule → cost-estimate" computation pipeline exists anywhere in the codebase yet, for any provider — that's cross-cutting PRD-051/053 infrastructure, not this PRD's job. I proved instead (with a real test) that this adapter records exactly the dimensions (resolved model, distinct token categories) such a pipeline needs, and that the existing append-only `cost_estimates`/`price_schedules` schema already accepts a correctly-computed `local-estimate` row keyed to a versioned, dated schedule.

**Testing:** 42 new tests, all passing; full existing suites for `familiar-ai-llm`, `familiar-ai-agent`, and `familiar-ai-daemon` (with `--no-default-features`) pass with no regressions; full workspace `cargo test --no-default-features` — 71/71 binaries green. `cargo fmt`/`clippy` clean on all touched code.

**Pre-existing, unrelated issues found (not caused by this work):**
- `cargo build`/`test` with default features fails to *link* `familiar-ai-daemon`'s binary (`-lxdo` missing) — the sandbox lacks the GTK/libxdo system libraries the `tray` feature needs. Verified with `--no-default-features`.
- `familiar_ai_core::bootstrap.rs` has one pre-existing `clippy::nonminimal_bool` warning.
- `codex::tests::bounded_execution_kills_a_timed_out_process` is flaky under parallel load (passes in isolation) — unrelated file, pre-existing timing sensitivity.

All PRD-060 acceptance criteria are met. No `FAMILIAR-INCOMPLETE` line is warranted.
