## Summary

PRD-061 (xAI Grok raw-API adapter) is implemented. Before writing code I verified xAI's real wire protocol against `docs.x.ai` (base URL, auth, streaming SSE shape, usage/cost fields, function-calling behavior, pricing) via live web fetches, since the acceptance criteria explicitly forbid declaring capabilities from OpenAI-protocol resemblance.

**Files created** (matching `expected_files`, minus one deliberate deviation):
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs` — `XaiAdapter: InferenceAdapter`, targeting `/v1/chat/completions` (fully documented streaming/usage/cost, unlike `/v1/responses` whose streaming event names aren't documented — see deviation note in the contract doc). 18 wiremock-backed tests.
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/xai.rs` — loop-facing glue: runtime/model-family constants and a `XAI_CAPABILITY_PROFILE` table with honest PRD-057 provenance (structured-output=`probed`, reasoning-controls=`unknown`, never `declared`).
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs` — 6 tests round-tripping the real adapter through the unmodified `run_loop` (whole-chunk tool call to completion, real wall-clock timeout, 5xx→ProviderFailure, auth-fails-closed, Grok price-schedule and cost-tick fixtures).
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/xai_adapter.rs` — 2 tests: full SQLite journal/evidence/PRD-051 ledger round-trip, and idempotent-replay-vs-separate-attempt at the accounting boundary.
- `docs/contracts/xai-adapter.md` — normative contract with the verification record, capability table, pricing, billing, and security sections.

**Deviation (documented in the contract doc's closing section):** `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/providers.rs` was left unmodified. Its `InferenceRuntimeKind` enum governs a different, narrower thing — self-hosted endpoint *discovery* (`unsloth`), wired only through `config_cli.rs`'s `provider add` command, which recognizes no other kind. PRD-057's actual worker-identity model already uses free, validated `provider`/`runtime` strings in `registry_workers.rs`, requiring no enum change — adding an unused `InferenceRuntimeKind::XaiApi` with no caller would be dead code.

**Verification:** `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets` clean on all touched crates (one pre-existing unrelated warning in `bootstrap.rs`); full test suites for `familiar-ai-llm` (94 passed), `familiar-ai-agent` (75 passed), and `familiar-ai-daemon` (all passed) — no regressions. `cargo check --workspace` type-checks cleanly. Note: building the `familiar-ai-daemon` *binary* with default features fails on a pre-existing missing system library (`libxdo`, for the tray icon) — confirmed identical on the unmodified baseline via a temporary stash; I tested with `--no-default-features` to route around it.

All 14 acceptance criteria are met, including the fixture list (whole-chunk streaming, partial streams, malformed arguments, rate limits, provider errors, cancellation, missing usage, alias drift, auth failure, retries, exactly-once accounting) with no live or billable call anywhere.
